"Read the Docs supports serving custom ``llms.txt`` files from your "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:14
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:16
msgid ""
"The ``llms.txt`` file will be served from the **default version** of your"
" project at ``https://your-project.readthedocs.io/llms.txt``. This is "
"because the ``llms.txt`` file is served at the top-level of your domain, "
"so we must choose a version to find the file in. The **default version** "
"is the best place to look for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:21
msgid ""
"If you also provide a ``llms-full.txt`` file, Read the Docs will serve it"
" from ``https://your-project.readthedocs.io/llms-full.txt`` using the "
"same rules."
msgstr ""

