msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:41
msgid ""
"Documentation tools will have different ways of generating a ``llms.txt``"
" file. We have examples for some of the most popular tools below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:46
msgid "Sphinx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:48
msgid ""
"Sphinx uses the `html_extra_path`_ configuration value to add static "
"files to its final HTML output. You need to create a ``llms.txt`` file "
"and put it under the path defined in ``html_extra_path``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:51
msgid ""
"You can also use the `sphinx-llm`_ extension to automatically generate an"
" ``llms.txt`` file from your documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:53
msgid "MkDocs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:55
msgid ""
"MkDocs needs the ``llms.txt`` to be at the directory defined by the "
"`docs_dir`_ configuration value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:57
msgid ""
"You can also use the `mkdocs-llmstxt`_ plugin to automatically generate "
"an ``llms.txt`` file from your documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:60
msgid "Alternative: Using redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/llms-txt.rst:62
msgid ""
"If you want to serve your ``llms.txt`` file from a versioned path (like "
"``/en/latest/llms.txt``), you can create an :doc:`exact redirect "
"</guides/redirects>` from ``/llms.txt`` to ``/en/latest/llms.txt``. This "
"gives you more control over which version serves the file."
msgstr ""

